===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|κένωσις||emptying|lang=grc}} (see [[keno-]] and [[κενό]]), from {{term|κενόειν||to empty|lang=grc}} (with reference to Philippians 2.vii, "But he emptied himself, taking the form of a slave, becoming as human beings are" – New Jerusalem Version).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kɪˈnəʊsɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|kenoses}}

# {{context|Christianity|lang=en}} [[Christ]]'s voluntary abasement consisting humanity and the simultaneous occultation of the Divinity.

